<section class="paper">
  <div class="wrap story">
    <div class="side rv">
      <span class="k mono">\ The brief</span>
      <h2>Imagine, illuminate, create: a full rebrand for <span class="serif">Flashpoint.</span></h2>
      <ul class="svc">
        {services.map((s) => <li><i>✳</i>{s}</li>)}
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="body rv">
      <p>Flashpoint is Adorama's private label: lighting and photography gear built to punch above its price, for pros and enthusiasts alike. Strong reputation, dated look. The project came through Art of Visuals, and I led it as Creative Director with Dannie Nicholson on art direction.</p>
      <p>Together we took the rebrand across four fronts at once: a fresh brand image and updated messaging, a new website, revamped packaging, and out-of-home with real reach. Two of those fronts were mine hands-on. I designed and built the new flashpointlighting.com, and I set up the brand's social channels.</p>
      <p>Six years on, the system is still earning its keep. The site is still live, the channels have passed 20,000 followers, and Flashpoint still reads like a name photographers trust.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="white">
  <div class="wrap triad" data-triad>
    <span class="k mono">\ The idea</span>
    <h2 class="triadhead" aria-label="Imagine Illuminate Create">
      <span class="tw">Imagine</span>
      <span class="tw">Illuminate</span>
      <span class="tw">Create</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="cdd">
      <div class="colA rv">
        <p>The objective: revitalize Flashpoint's market presence and make the name synonymous with innovation, quality, and value in the world of photography.</p>
        <p>This was a top-to-bottom effort: a fresh brand image, sharper messaging, and a visual identity that could carry across every surface, from the box on the shelf to the billboard on the street. The four fronts below are how it shipped, and they are the chapters of this file.</p>
      </div>
